# 8-bit Accumulator-Based CPU

## Overview
This project implements an 8-bit accumulator-based CPU using structural VHDL in Xilinx ISE. It supports basic arithmetic and logical operations using a predefined instruction set.

## Features
- 4-bit Program Counter (PC)
- Instruction ROM and Decoder
- Control Unit
- 8-bit ALU
- Accumulator Register (ACC)
- Multiplexer (MUX)
- Zero Flag detection
- Simulation using Xilinx ISE (ISim)

## Instruction Set

| Opcode | Instruction | Operation |
|---|---|---|
| `0001` | LDI | Load immediate |
| `0010` | ADD | ACC + Immediate |
| `0011` | SUB | ACC − Immediate |
| `0100` | AND | ACC AND Immediate |
| `0101` | OR | ACC OR Immediate |

## Tools Used
- VHDL
- Xilinx ISE
- ISim Simulator

## Simulation
The CPU executes a predefined program stored in ROM. The testbench verifies accumulator results and zero flag behavior.

